{{also|rétrospective}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|retrospect|-ive}}. From {{der|en|la|retrōspectus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|retrōspiciō||I look back at}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɹɛtɹə(ʊ)ˈspɛktɪv/}}
* {{audio|en|en-GB-retrospective.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛktɪv}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, relating to, or [[contemplating]] the [[past]].
#* '''2015''', Louise Taylor, ''Papiss Cissé and Jonny Evans spitting row mars Manchester United’s win over Newcastle'' (in ''The Guardian'', 4 March 2015)[http://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/mar/04/newcastle-united-manchester-united-premier-league-match-report]
#*: While the pictures of what precisely unfolded after Cissé looked to tread on Evans are not entirely conclusive, the Football Association will surely pore over them on Thursday before quite possibly using video evidence to impose lengthy '''retrospective''' bans stemming from an incident unseen by Anthony Taylor, the referee.
# [[looking|Looking]] [[backwards]].
# [[affect|Affecting]] or [[influencing]] past things; [[retroactive]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|hindsightly}}

